        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State of Texas in this case claims the right to criminally punish any unmarried adult couple for engaging in any form of consensual sexual intimacy that the State happens to disapprove of."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Smith",
      "case_id": "2002-02-102",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06bfc57f1c47b1564a4df22da5156e9c1503b36f0f4ff3865315dd4156c293c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06bfc57f1c47-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We certainly do not think we do, Your Honor. We think this fails rational basis scrutiny, just as the law did in Romer, in Cleburne, in Moreno, in Eisenstadt, all of those laws were thrown out under rational basis scrutiny, because the State basically didn't come up with anything other than we want it that way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-02-102",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06bfc57f1c47b1564a4df22da5156e9c1503b36f0f4ff3865315dd4156c293c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06bfc57f1c47-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: We said the opposite in Bowers, didn't we?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Smith",
      "case_id": "2002-02-102",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06bfc57f1c47b1564a4df22da5156e9c1503b36f0f4ff3865315dd4156c293c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06bfc57f1c47-0001-0002",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "People in the States who still regulate sodomy everyday they're denied visitation to their own children, they're denied custody of children, they're denied public employment. They're denied private employment, because they're labeled as criminals merely because they've been identified as homosexuals."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rosenthal",
      "case_id": "2002-02-102",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06bfc57f1c47b1564a4df22da5156e9c1503b36f0f4ff3865315dd4156c293c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06bfc57f1c47-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State humbly submits that enforcement of Texas Penal Code Statute 21.06 does not violate the 14th Amendment of the Constitution because this Court has never recognized a fundamental right to engage in extramarital sexual conduct and because there is a rational basis for the statute sufficient to withstand equal protection scrutiny."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2002-02-102",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06bfc57f1c47b1564a4df22da5156e9c1503b36f0f4ff3865315dd4156c293c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06bfc57f1c47-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: Very well, Mr. Smith. Mr. Rosenthal, we'll hear from you."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-02-102",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06bfc57f1c47b1564a4df22da5156e9c1503b36f0f4ff3865315dd4156c293c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06bfc57f1c47-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Why -- why do you think that the public perception of -- of homosexual acts has -- has not changed? Do you think it hasn't?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Unknown Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-02-102",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06bfc57f1c47b1564a4df22da5156e9c1503b36f0f4ff3865315dd4156c293c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06bfc57f1c47-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "QUESTION: Does Texas prohibit sexual intercourse between unmarried heterosexuals?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Texas",
      "case_id": "2002-02-102",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06bfc57f1c47b1564a4df22da5156e9c1503b36f0f4ff3865315dd4156c293c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06bfc57f1c47-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "under the equal protection argument, Texas has the right to set moral standards and can set bright line moral standards for its people. And in the setting of those moral standards, I believe that they can say that certain kinds of activity can exist and certain kinds of activity cannot exist."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2002-02-102",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06bfc57f1c47b1564a4df22da5156e9c1503b36f0f4ff3865315dd4156c293c2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06bfc57f1c47-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: Thank you Mr. Smith. The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
